upstream.json is the machine-readable build pin. install.sh verifies the
archive before extracting, applies upstream.patch with -p1, and builds using
the upstream Cargo.lock. upstream.patch is maintained downstream; the staged
binary is modified software, not an unmodified upstream release. This source
archive pin does not claim that transitive dependencies have been vendored.

The Python launch helpers and build recipe are downstream additions by
Smarty Pants, Inc. They do not install or activate the upstream Reviewr HerdR
plugin, contact upstream maintainers, or alter HerdR fleet state. The existing
Explorr local-file link handler launches the patched viewer. Preserve this
notice and the MIT license when redistributing the binary or helper bundle.
